  positive on both, direction="up". Consistent.
- round2()'s structural property (internal/services/mcpsvc/spend/insights.go
  round2 = math.Round(v*100)/100) cannot flip a sign class: positive input
  never rounds to negative output and vice versa (only collapses toward
  zero). Verified with hostile synthetic rows through categoryTrendRows --
  no case produced roundedCA and roundedCP with opposite nonzero signs;
  Direction is taken from the pre-rounding classification, not re-derived
  from the rounded percent, so display-time rounding cannot reintroduce the
  sign inversion this task closes. (Noted, not a FAIL: raw values very close
  to zero can independently round to "-0"/"0" on the two fields when
  |previous| is sub-cent -- mathematically inert for this contract and not
  reachable by any real major-expense figure in this ledger; flagged as a
  pre-existing display nuance, out of CB3-c's scope, not a defect in it.)

